- `createGame(boardCode)` returns an immutable game state or `null`; board metadata
  is `state.board.boardCode` and `state.board.size`.
- State also exposes immutable `deck` and `matched`, `selection`, `moves`,
  `elapsedMs` and `started`. Selection is a closed/one/mismatch union.
- `activateCard(state, index)` and `advanceGame(state, milliseconds)` return new
  immutable state when an action advances it. `advanceGame` accepts finite
  fractional active milliseconds, caps elapsed display at 359999999, and continues
  a pending mismatch timer even after the elapsed cap.
- `encodeSnapshot(state)` emits indented v1 JSON, floors elapsed milliseconds and
  rounds pending mismatch time up to at least 1ms. `decodeSnapshot(text)` and
  `replayGame(text)` return a validated state or `null`.
- `GAME_LIMITS`, `BOARD_SIZES`, `matchedPairCount`, `isWon` and `formatTime` are
  exported from their defining modules. The CLI is `npm run --silent replay -- PATH`.
- CLI tests cover stdout/exit behavior for valid, malformed and unreadable input.

## Session interface handoff

- `useGameSession()` in `src/game/session/useGameSession.ts` returns
  `game`, `dealId`, `paused`, `best`, `celebrating`, `status`,
  `announcement: {serial, text}`, and methods `activateCard(index)`,
  `newGame()`, `restart()`, `changeSize(size)`, `loadBoard(draft)`,
  `loadSnapshot(draft)`, `exportSnapshot()`, and `resume()`.
- `dealId` increments only for a new deal, restart, size change, or successful
  board/snapshot import. Card and clock updates leave it alone, so UI drafts and
  remembered board focus can remain stable through ordinary play.
- `status` carries the visible reproduction-control result; each turn/load
  announcement increments its independent `serial`, even for repeated identical
  text. The UI owns the single atomic polite live region.
- `resume()` removes the pause; its click handler should focus the board's
  remembered card before calling it because the Resume button disappears.
- Session time uses an injected monotonic clock. The mismatch deadline runs
  against remaining active time and is canceled on hide, pause, deal replacement,
  and cleanup. Timer callbacks check generations and deal identity.
- `npm test` passes 35 tests and `npm run typecheck` passes after the session
  changes.


## UI interface handoff

- `Game.tsx` composes the session hook, native deal controls, status, board, and collapsed reproduction controls.
- `Board` in `src/game/board/Board.tsx` keeps one roving `tabIndex`, returns a focus handle for Resume, clamps arrow navigation without wrapping, and scrolls each focused card into view with nearest alignment.
- `describeFace(id)` in `src/game/board/face.ts` exports all 128 ordered shapes/markers/fills/colors and exact lowercase face names; `FaceArtwork` mounts only for revealed/matched cards. Hidden cards contain only a common neutral diamond.
- CSS Grid columns use the scroll container width and clamp each square card between 44px and 88px. The page passed checks at 360×800 and 1280×800 without outer horizontal overflow.
- Reproduction draft stays in component state until a deal changes. Snapshot export uses the session sync and readable JSON. The UI has one polite atomic live region keyed by announcement serial and a visible reproduction status.
- `npm test` passes 40 tests across 11 files; `npm run build` includes a passing `npm run typecheck`. Playwright screenshots: `evidence/ui/desktop.png` and `evidence/ui/phone.png`; 16×16 variants are alongside them. The temporary preview server is stopped.
