## Core interface handoff

- `createGame(boardCode)` returns an immutable game state or `null`; board metadata
  is `state.board.boardCode` and `state.board.size`.
- State also exposes immutable `deck` and `matched`, `selection`, `moves`,
  `elapsedMs` and `started`. Selection is a closed/one/mismatch union.
- `activateCard(state, index)` and `advanceGame(state, milliseconds)` return new
  immutable state when an action advances it. `advanceGame` accepts finite
  fractional active milliseconds, caps elapsed display at 359999999, and continues
  a pending mismatch timer even after the elapsed cap.
- `encodeSnapshot(state)` emits indented v1 JSON, floors elapsed milliseconds and
  rounds pending mismatch time up to at least 1ms. `decodeSnapshot(text)` and
  `replayGame(text)` return a validated state or `null`.
- `GAME_LIMITS`, `BOARD_SIZES`, `matchedPairCount`, `isWon` and `formatTime` are
  exported from their defining modules. The CLI is `npm run --silent replay -- PATH`.
- CLI tests cover stdout/exit behavior for valid, malformed and unreadable input.

